*            / \
*           15  7
*
* Step 1: height(9) = 1
* Step 2: height(20) = 2
* Step 3: |1 - 2| = 1 → Balanced
* Step 4: Check subtrees (both balanced)
* ✅ Output: true
***************************************************************************************************
* ⚙️ EDGE CASES:
* 1️⃣ Empty tree → balanced (returns true)
* 2️⃣ Single node → balanced (true)
* 3️⃣ Skewed tree (all left or all right nodes) → unbalanced (false)
*
* Example Unbalanced Tree:
*     1
*    /
*   2
*  /
* 3
* → height(left)=2, height(right)=0 → |2|>1 → false
***************************************************************************************************
* ⏱️ TIME COMPLEXITY: O(N²)
* Reason: For every node, height() runs in O(N), and we call it for each node.
*
* 💾 SPACE COMPLEXITY: O(H)
* Reason: Recursive call stack where H = height of tree.
